# Registry target for `bun publish` (issue #884). package.json's
# `publishConfig.registry` documents the same target for tooling that reads
# it, but `bun publish` itself (bun 1.3.x) only resolves the registry/auth
# from .npmrc / bunfig.toml / --registry — it does NOT read
# publishConfig.registry. This file is the one that actually drives CI's
# publish step; keep both in sync if the registry ever changes.
#
# GitHub Packages requires the scope to match the GitHub org/user that owns
# the repository being published from (`robotmoney`), which is already the
# `@robotmoney` scope this package publishes under.
@robotmoney:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}
